{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.QuantumDilogarithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.QuantumDilogarithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qInteger_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qInteger_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L94-L100","doc":"For q > 1, [1]_q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qDilog_first_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qDilog_first_term","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L87-L92","doc":"The first term of the quantum dilogarithm is `z / [1]_q = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qDilog_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qDilog_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L78-L85","doc":"The quantum dilogarithm is non-negative at z = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qDilogPartialSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qDilogPartialSum","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L72-L76","doc":"The partial sum of the quantum dilogarithm series at `z`:\n`Σ_{k=1}^{N} (-1)^{k+1} z^k / (k [k]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qDilogCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qDilogCoeff","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The `n`-th coefficient of the quantum dilogarithm series:\n`(-1)^{n+1} / (n · [n]_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.qInteger","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The q-integer `[n]_q = (qⁿ - 1)/(q - 1)` for `q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.q_param","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.R_q","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/quantum-dilogarithm.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0}]}